![OpenAI](https://img.shields.io/badge/AI-OpenAI%20GPT--4o-green.svg)

## 📌 About The Project

This project implements an autonomous closed-loop control system for Material Extrusion (MEX/FDM) 3D printers. By capturing spatial and visual data of individual printing layers, the system uses Vision-Language Models (VLMs) like GPT-4o to evaluate print quality in real-time. If defects such as warping, stringing, or inconsistent extrusion are detected, the system dynamically adjusts printing parameters (e.g., flow rate, speed, temperature, Z-offset) via the Moonraker API.

Traditional open-loop systems fail to correct issues on the fly. This architecture bridges the gap by providing zero-shot reasoning capabilities to diagnose and deploy immediate corrective actions without the need for extensive dataset-dependent Deep Learning model fine-tuning.

### ✨ Key Features
* **Real-time Defect Detection:** Layer-by-layer (or intermittent) visual inspection to catch stringing, warping, and under/over-extrusion.
* **Autonomous Parameter Adjustment:** Dynamically modifies print speed, extrusion multiplier, and temperatures via JSON-structured API commands.
* **Sensor-Agnostic AI Reasoning:** Utilizes VLMs (GPT-4o) for high-tier reasoning and contextual understanding of print anomalies.
* **Security Whitelist:** Implements a strict JSON parsing and security whitelist to prevent the AI from executing dangerous commands or halting the printer entirely.

## 🛠 Hardware & Software Stack

### Hardware Requirements
* **3D Printer:** Any FDM/MEX printer running Klipper firmware.
* **Host Machine:** Raspberry Pi 4 (4GB RAM recommended) or standard PC.
* **Camera:** Intel RealSense D435 (or standard high-resolution RGB webcams).

### Software Requirements
* **Firmware/API:** Klipper + Moonraker API
* **Language:** Python 3.9+
* **AI Model:** OpenAI API (GPT-4o)

## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites
1. Ensure your 3D printer is correctly set up with **Klipper** and **Moonraker**.
2. Obtain an API key from [OpenAI](https://platform.openai.com/).
